    "b-ks2-src-attempts-intro": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "ATTEMPTS — The attempt source is not a new table: it is the target ledger wearing its evidence hat. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker_run",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows, their submissions, and their archived transcripts are the store behind "
        },
        {
          "insert": "attempt://",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " locators. Operational class — the store grows with every run, and rows and artifacts are immutable once written, so an attempt locator cannot drift and carries no digest."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-ks2-src-attempts-intro",
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-attempts-grammar-heading": {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Locator grammar"
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-ks2-src-attempts-grammar-heading",
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-attempts-grammar-body": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "attempt://run/<worker_run.id>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " resolves to the run itself. Appending "
        },
        {
          "insert": "/submission/<seq>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " narrows to one submission by its sequence within the run; appending "
        },
        {
          "insert": "/transcript/<span>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " narrows to a span of the run's archived transcript. The grammar is closed: the resolver rejects any other shape, and rejects a submission or span the run does not have."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-ks2-src-attempts-grammar-body",
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-attempts-ownership": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The tables and artifacts are owned by the target ledger: shape, writers, and lifecycle live in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Worker Runs",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/40-knowledge/20-record-contracts/30-target-ledger/10-worker-runs",
              "label": "Worker Runs"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". This page defines only how the knowledge graph cites into them."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-ks2-src-attempts-ownership",
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-attempts-search-heading": {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Search surface"
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-ks2-src-attempts-search-heading",
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-attempts-search-body": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Structured first: filters by target, outcome, score trajectory, and epoch, because attempt retrieval usually starts from a known target. BM25 runs over hypotheses and transcripts for the rest. There is no vector surface — deliberately. Vectors are added later only if lexical retrieval demonstrably misses; until then the surface stays structured and keyword only."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-ks2-src-attempts-search-body",
      "children": []
    },
